      "id": 1,
      "text": "Penfield was named after pioneer Hoyt, whose reputedly excellent penmanship earned the village its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mtzionhistoricalsociety.org/history/stories/penfield-the-head-of-bennetts-valley-branch/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1873 the Low Grade railroad, running from Driftwood to Red Bank, reached Penfield, linking the town to regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mtzionhistoricalsociety.org/history/stories/penfield-the-head-of-bennetts-valley-branch/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers celebrated services barefoot, wearing red bandanas as headwear, a tradition that echoed the community’s humble roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mtzionhistoricalsociety.org/history/stories/penfield-the-head-of-bennetts-valley-branch/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Surveyor Lucien Bird noted ax marks on trees dated 1729, suggesting Jesuit activity in the area long before the Revolution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mtzionhistoricalsociety.org/history/stories/penfield-the-head-of-bennetts-valley-branch/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Penfield sits at the crossroads of Pennsylvania Routes 153 and 255, 11.3 miles east‑northeast of DuBois.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penfield%2C_Pennsylvania",
